list.item:
This deponent saw the cargo transferred from the schooner to the steamer
                        as aforesaid, and assisted therein, and he knows of his own knowledge that
                        it consisted of about rive hundred cases of shot, shell, and ammunition;
                        over one hundred cases of arms; two or threedozen boxes of leather goods;
                        adozen or so of caps; about six carriages for guns; and six or eight boxes
                        of hardware. There were also four brass cannon.
